            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention discloses a spinal cord stimulator device implantable in a patient's tissue comprising an electrode array with a plurality of electrodes, the spinal cord stimulator device further comprising control circuitry configured to: provide pulses during different time periods, wherein during each time period pulses are provided to three or more pole locations in the electrode array, wherein a cathodic pulse is provided at one of the pole locations and anodic pulses are provided at two or more of the pole locations during each of the different time periods, and wherein the cathodic pulse is moved to different of the pole locations during at least some of the different time periods, preferably during each of the different time periods.</p>
            </abstract>
